 "intro_html": "The onigiri with the meat on the <b>outside</b>: little barrels of rice wrapped in paper-thin <b>pork belly</b>, dusted with cornstarch, fried in sesame oil until the pork is golden and crisp, then rolled in a soy, sake and mirin glaze with garlic and ginger until they shine. It started as a staff meal at an onigiri shop in Miyazaki in the late 1990s and went national. Cook the rice as for <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a> — plain short-grain rice, still warm. Two each makes a meal, one a snack.",
