 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Divide the warm rice into six <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> portions.</li><li>Wet your hands and shape each into a little <b>barrel</b> (tawara), about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"6\" data-b=\"7\" data-s=\"0\">6–7 cm</span> long.</li><li>Press firmly enough that it holds together, but don't crush the rice.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Shape the rice barrels",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wet your hands and shape 50 g of rice into a little barrel.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/1-how1.webp?v=f810abcc9d"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/1.webp?v=741000835a",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Shape the rice barrels",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"300\">300 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Cooked Japanese short-grain rice"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lay a slice of pork belly on the board and set a barrel on it, pointing the same way as the slice.</li><li>Wrap the slice <b>lengthways</b> around the barrel — under it, up over one end, along the top, over the other end and back to the start. Rice still shows on the two long sides.</li><li>Snip off the excess with scissors and keep it for the next step.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap lengthways",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stand the barrel on the slice and take the slice up over the top end, and down the other side.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/2-how1.webp?v=a2a8c90abb"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Snip off the excess with scissors.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/2-how2.webp?v=f52fea0e54"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/2.webp?v=c5c9683b45",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~4 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~4 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap lengthways",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"9\" data-n=\"1\">9</span> long slices",
     "name_html": "Pork belly, thinly sliced"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wrap the trimmed piece plus half a slice the <b>other way</b>, round the middle, until no rice shows anywhere.</li><li>Each ball takes about 1½ slices. Pull the pork snug — any gap lets the rice fall out in the pan.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap round the middle",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wrap the trimmed piece and half a slice round the middle until no rice shows.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/3-how1.webp?v=1c16e73ac5"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/3.webp?v=5d080c2074",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap round the middle",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Spread the cornstarch on a plate.</li><li>Roll each wrapped ball in it for a thin, even coat, then tap off the excess — it makes the pork crisp and thickens the glaze later.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Dust with cornstarch",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Roll each ball in the cornstarch, then tap off the excess.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/4-how1.webp?v=6b194ce3a3"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/4.webp?v=125148195c",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~1 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min</span>",
   "title": "Dust with cornstarch",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Cornstarch (or potato starch)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir together in a small bowl:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>soy sauce</li><li>sake</li><li>mirin</li><li>sugar</li><li>ginger, grated</li><li>garlic, grated</li></ul></li><li>Or mix it while the balls fry.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix the glaze",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Stir the glaze together.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/5-how1.webp?v=46a6ccde6e"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/5.webp?v=625e4ac2f2",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~2 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~2 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix the glaze",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat the sesame oil in a large frying pan over <b>medium</b> heat.</li><li>Put the balls in with the <b>seam side down</b> — it seals the wrap.</li><li>Fry, turning every minute or so, until golden and crisp on every side and the pork is cooked through, about 6–8 minutes.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fry until crisp",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Seam side down first — it seals the wrap.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/6-how1.webp?v=38f82009d2"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Turn every minute or so until golden and crisp on every side.",
      "src": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/6-how2.webp?v=62f29ee862"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/nikumaki-onigiri/6.webp?v=2e120e81d7",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~6–8 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~6–8 min</span>",
   "title": "Fry until crisp",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Toasted sesame oil"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wipe the fat out of the pan with kitchen paper.</li><li>Turn the heat to <b>high</b> and pour in the glaze.</li><li>Keep rolling the balls until the sauce boils down to a thick, sticky glaze that coats them all over, 1–2 minutes. If it thickens too fast, turn the heat down — it burns quickly.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "high",
    "label_html": "<span>high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
